        <https://w3id.org/cdisc/cosmos/bc/C191036/dec/C82556> ;
    cosmos_bc:definition "A standardized clinical tool, published in 1980 by Harvey et al. as a simplified version of the Crohn Disease Activity Index (CDAI), that assesses and scores five patient parameters (well-being, abdominal pain, number of liquid or soft stools, abdominal mass, and complications) to stratify Crohn's disease severity." ;
